[\n\\mathcal L_k=\\{V_1,\\dots ,V_{\\,n-k}\\}\\cup\\{L_1,\\dots ,L_k\\}.\n\\]\n\nAll \\(V_j\\) are vertical, hence not sunny; each \\(L_i\\) has slope \\(+1\\neq0,\\infty,-1\\), so every \\(L_i\\) is sunny.  The lines are distinct because the \\(V_j\\) have different \\(x\\)-coordinates and the \\(L_i\\) have different constant terms \\(-(n-k+i-1)\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n#### Verification that \\(\\mathcal L_k\\) covers \\(T_n\\)\n\nTake an arbitrary point \\((a,b)\\in T_n\\).\n\n*Case 1: \\(a\\le n-k\\).*  \nThen \\((a,b)\\) lies on the vertical line \\(V_a\\).\n\n*Case 2: \\(a\\ge n-k+1\\).*  \nSet  \n\n\\[\na' = a-(n-k),\\qquad b' = b .\n\\]\n\nFrom \\(a+b\\le n+1\\) we obtain  \n\n\\[\na'+b' = a+b-(n-k)\\le (n+1)-(n-k)=k+1,\n\\]\nand clearly \\(1\\le a',b'\\le k\\) (because \\(a\\le n\\) and \\(b\\le n+1-a\\le k\\)).\nHence \\((a',b')\\) belongs to the rectangle  \n\n\\[\nR_k=\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb Z_{>0}^2\\mid 1\\le x\\le k,\\;1\\le y\\le k\\}.\n\\]\n\nDefine  \n\n\\[\ni = a'-b'+1 .\n\\]\n\nSince \\(1\\le a',b'\\le k\\), the integer \\(i\\) satisfies \\(1\\le i\\le k\\).\nNow  \n\n\\[\nb' = a'-i+1,\n\\]\n\nso \\((a',b')\\) lies on the line \\(\\ell_i\\) of Lemma 1.  Translating back to\nthe original coordinates gives  \n\n\\[\nb = a-(n-k+i-1),\n\\]\n\ni.e. \\((a,b)\\) lies on the sunny line \\(L_i\\).\n\nThus every point of \\(T_n\\) belongs to at least one line of\n\\(\\mathcal L_k\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n#### Counting sunny lines\n\n\\(\\mathcal L_k\\) contains exactly the \\(k\\) lines \\(L_1,\\dots ,L_k\\), all\nof which are sunny, and the remaining \\(n-k\\) lines are vertical (not\nsunny).  Hence the number of sunny lines is precisely \\(k\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n#### Conclusion\n\nFor each integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n\\) we have exhibited a set of\n\\(n\\) distinct lines that\n\n* cover every lattice point \\((a,b)\\) with \\(a,b>0\\) and \\(a+b\\le n+1\\);\n* contain exactly \\(k\\) sunny lines.\n\nTherefore the set of admissible values of \\(k\\) is  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{0,1,2,\\dots ,n}.\n\\] ∎\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
